
Subject: [PATCH] ne10: allow configuring under CMake 4

Buildroot 2026.02 builds host-cmake 4.2.3, which removed support for
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION <3.5). Ne10 1.2.1 declares 2.6 at
CMakeLists.txt:27, so it now fails to configure:

  CMake Error at CMakeLists.txt:27 (cmake_minimum_required):
    Compatibility with CMake < 3.5 has been removed from CMake.

Ne10 is upstream-dead (last release 2018), so bumping the declaration in
the source is not going to come from there. Raise it to 3.5, the lowest
version CMake 4 still accepts; Ne10's CMakeLists.txt does not rely on
anything dropped between 2.6 and 3.5, so this is a no-op for the actual
build. Ne10 is selected by package/DATV, so without this fix any
defconfig that enables DATV cannot build.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
 #  (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE OF THIS
 #  SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.
 #
-cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 2.6)
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.5)

 project(NE10 C ASM)
